{"page": 3, "kind": "cell", "table": 1, "row": 9, "col": 3, "x": null, "text": "Content Standard SS.MHH.1.19.1 Examine the long-term causes and triggering events, people, and ideas behind the overthrow of the Hawaiian monarchy", "id": "u46", "furniture": false}
{"page": 3, "kind": "cell", "table": 1, "row": 9, "col": 4, "x": null, "text": "• Long-Term Causes: Bayonet Constitution, cultural imperialism, increasing economic dependence on U.S., Māhele, Reciprocity Treaty of 1875 • Triggering Events, People, and Ideas: foreign movement against Kalākaua, John Stevens, Liliʻuokalani and the Bayonet Constitution, Lorrin Thurston, Sanford Dole • Arguments for and Against the Overthrow: monarchy v. democracy, naval base, sovereignty, sugar profits", "id": "u47", "furniture": false}
{"page": 3, "kind": "cell", "table": 1, "row": 10, "col": 1, "x": null, "text": "Anchor Standard 19", "id": "u48", "furniture": false}
